kosha iron

  -- Fe. proton-26. period 4, transition metal. valence: 2 or 3 (Fe²⁺, Fe³⁺).
  -- most used structural metal. core of the earth is iron-nickel.
  -- ferromagnetic: iron, cobalt, nickel are the only room-temperature ferromagnets.
  -- haemoglobin: Fe²⁺ at centre of porphyrin ring — binds and releases O2.
  -- steel: iron + carbon (0.02–2.1%). cast iron >2.1% carbon.
  -- rusting: 4Fe + 3O2 + 6H2O → 4Fe(OH)3 → Fe2O3·nH2O (oxidation).
  -- most abundant element on earth by mass (32% of earth's total mass).

